  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Hermann Rorschach was a Swiss psychiatrist and psychoanalyst, who, in 1918, began working on a test that would be used for years to come in the field of psychology. The Rorschach Inkblot tests were influenced by the game Blotto, which was popular during Rorschach’s youth. These inkblots were developed further over the years and became an important tool in identifying patients who may be at risk for mental disorders. This book was created in a time that was filled with transformation, reflection, self-evaluation, and a good dose of psychoanalysis. While it may have its own story, the interpretation is left open to the viewer, just like in Rorschach’s original cards" -- Artist's statement.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="586" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artist's book by SCAD Graphic Design student Sarah Nelson. What Rorschach Told Me was awarded an honorable mention in the 8th Annual Juried Student Artist's Book Competition by Juror Jay Fox.</subfield>
